OVERVIEW: Decode a JP3D volumetric document back to individual DICOM slices

Reads a JP3D DICOM document, decodes the JP3D codestream, and writes one
DICOM file per slice into the output directory.

Output files are named slice_0000.dcm, slice_0001.dcm, …

Example:
  dicom-3d decode-volume volume.jp3d.dcm --output ./decoded/

USAGE: dicom-3d decode-volume <input-path> --output <output> [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <input-path>            JP3D DICOM document file to decode

OPTIONS:
  -o, --output <output>   Output directory for decoded DICOM slices
  --verbose               Verbose output
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

